-- fallback.talk: a Fallback Handler and a spread in `send … with` (ADR
-- 0064). Part of the messages-and-waiting case. Each Fallback clause is a
-- `fallback` body named `any message`, with the message map as its one
-- parameter. A spreading `send` builds its arguments as one list, under the
-- name as text, and ends in `send-spread`, `send-spread-wait` or
-- `join-send-spread`.

on relay rest
  send log with "seen", ...rest to me
  send ("move:to:") with ...rest to me and wait
  wait for all
    send (the name of it) with ...rest, 1 to me and wait
  end wait
end relay

on any message {name: n, args: a} where n begins with "debug"
  send (n) with ...a to me
end any message

on any message m, queued
  pass any message
end
